    "low_level": "Both recipients run the released original SONIC decoder on their own live 930-value proprioceptive/action history each control tick. Native motors, contact dynamics and termination run in corrected Bullet.",
    "direct_V4": "The frozen V4 actor reads three current native Bullet-state RGB views at 128x96 (rendered through the common MuJoCo renderer), current robot proprioception and previous applied hands. It predicts five integer body-code and two-hand rows every five ticks. No agent-local rollout.",
    "optical_clock": "An external actor estimates object XY, pad XY and square yaw from three calibrated 320x240 recipient reset views; prior nominal mass, friction and standard standing pose initialize its local approximate MuJoCo. The same V4 actor uses live local RGB/proprioception to generate a full 750-tick native body/hand plan, including rows beyond any local success. The recipient takes time-matched five-row blocks until its own first terminal; the final block uses rows 745\u2013749 when the horizon is reached. After reset no new recipient observation changes the planned body or finger commands. No donor seed, privileged pose or prerecorded other-start tape is supplied.",
    "camera_names": [
      "overview",
      "hand",
      "side"
    ]
  },
